  "response": "## Analyse\n\nJe vais créer `tests/test_summarize.py` avec 4 tests couvrant les cas limites : texte vide, texte court, texte long, et max_sentences=1. D'abord, je valide l'import du module `tools.summarize`.\n\n**Validation préalable** :\n```bash\npython -c \"import tools.summarize; print('Import OK')\"\n```\n\nEnsuite, je génère les tests avec pytest, puis je valide la syntaxe et la collecte.\n\n---\n\n## Code\n\n```python path: tests/test_summarize.py\nimport pytest\nfrom tools.summarize import summarize, split_sentences, score_sentence\n\n\nclass TestSummarize:\n    \"\"\"Test suite for the summarize utility.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_empty_text(self):\n        \"\"\"Test summarize with empty text.\"\"\"\n        result = summarize(\"\")\n        assert result == \"\"\n\n    def test_short_text_below_max_sentences(self):\n        \"\"\"Test summarize with text shorter than max_sentences.\"\"\"\n        text = \"This is sentence one. This is sentence two.\"\n        result = summarize(text, max_sentences=5)\n        # Should return the full text (or close to it)\n        assert len(result) > 0\n        assert \"sentence one\" in result or \"sentence two\" in result\n\n    def test_long_text_with_default_max_sentences(self):\n        \"\"\"Test summarize with long text and default max_sentences.\"\"\"\n        text = \". \".join([f\"Sentence {i}\" for i in range(1, 11)]) + \".\"\n        result = summarize(text)\n        # Result should be shorter than input\n        assert len(result) < len(text)\n        assert len(result) > 0\n\n    def test_max_sentences_equals_one(self):\n        \"\"\"Test summarize with max_sentences=1.\"\"\"\n        text = \"First sentence. Second sentence. Third sentence.\"\n        result = summarize(text, max_sentences=1)\n        # Should return exactly one sentence (or close approximation)\n        assert len(result) > 0\n        assert result.count(\".\") >= 1\n\n\nclass TestSplitSentences:\n    \"\"\"Test suite for the split_sentences utility.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_split_empty_string(self):\n        \"\"\"Test split_sentences with empty string.\"\"\"\n        result = split_sentences(\"\")\n        assert result == []\n\n    def test_split_single_sentence(self):\n        \"\"\"Test split_sentences with single sentence.\"\"\"\n        result = split_sentences(\"Hello world.\")\n        assert len(result) > 0\n\n    def test_split_multiple_sentences(self):\n        \"\"\"Test split_sentences with multiple sentences.\"\"\"\n        text = \"First. Second. Third.\"\n        result = split_sentences(text)\n        assert len(result) >= 2\n\n\nclass TestScoreSentence:\n    \"\"\"Test suite for the score_sentence utility.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_score_empty_sentence(self):\n        \"\"\"Test score_sentence with empty sentence.\"\"\"\n        result = score_sentence(\"\")\n        assert isinstance(result, (int, float))\n\n    def test_score_normal_sentence(self):\n        \"\"\"Test score_sentence with normal sentence.\"\"\"\n        result = score_sentence(\"This is a test sentence.\")\n        assert isinstance(result, (int, float))\n        assert result >= 0\n```\n\n---\n\n## Validation\n\n```bash\n# 1. Valider l'import du module\npython -c \"import tools.summarize; print('✓ Import OK')\"\n\n# 2. Valider la syntaxe du fichier test\npython -m py_compile tests/test_summarize.py && echo \"✓ Syntaxe OK\"\n\n# 3. Collecter les tests\npytest tests/test_summarize.py --collect-only -q\n\n# 4. Exécuter les tests\npytest tests/test_summarize.py -v --tb=short\n```",
